<section id="deck">
  <h2>The Story Deck</h2><p class="source-note">Pages 14–15 and 18–19</p><p>The deck contains 16 numbered story-element cards and 3 Grey Ladies. Each card becomes one scene.</p>
  <div class="grid-5"><div class="card story-type clue"><h3>Clue</h3><p>Reveals something about the mystery: its nature, location, history, or signs.</p><p class="note">No roll by default.</p></div><div class="card story-type harmed"><h3>Secondary character harmed</h3><p>Someone other than the protagonist suffers physical, mental, or uncanny harm.</p><p class="note">Invent a fitting victim and consequence.</p></div><div class="card story-type character"><h3>Secondary character obstructs</h3><p>Another person actively hinders the protagonist through force, persuasion, deceit, authority, or warning.</p><p class="note"><strong>Obstacle: roll.</strong></p></div><div class="card story-type environment"><h3>Environment obstructs</h3><p>The landscape, weather, animals, terrain, accident, or circumstance gets in the way.</p><p class="note"><strong>Obstacle: roll.</strong></p></div><div class="card story-type grey"><h3>Grey Lady</h3><p>A major turning point. Use the next entry on the scenario’s Tension Table, then pay the cost.</p><p class="note">Tension permanently rises.</p></div></div>
</section>

<section id="setup">
  <h2>Set up the game</h2><p class="source-note">Pages 15–16</p>
  <div class="grid-2"><div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">1</div><div><h3>Choose a scenario</h3><p>Read its synopsis, characters, story elements, Tension Table, and Spirit Table.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">2</div><div><h3>Build the protagonist</h3><p>Complete the play sheet and place Spirit and Resolve tokens in front of you.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">3</div><div><h3>Prepare the Story Deck</h3><p>Put the Grey Ladies aside. Shuffle the other 16 cards and divide them into piles of <strong>5, 5, and 6</strong>.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">4</div><div><h3>Bury the Grey Ladies</h3><p>Put one Grey Lady beneath each pile. Stack the piles with the <strong>six-card pile at the bottom</strong>.</p></div></div></div><div class="card"><span class="label">Ordinary playing cards</span><p>Use three Queens as the Grey Ladies, plus the 4, 5, 6, and 7 from every suit.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table class="compact"><thead><tr><th>Suit</th><th>Story element</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>♥ Hearts</td><td>Secondary character harmed</td></tr><tr><td>♣ Clubs</td><td>Secondary character obstructs</td></tr><tr><td>♦ Diamonds</td><td>Environment obstructs</td></tr><tr><td>♠ Spades</td><td>Clue</td></tr><tr><td>3 Queens</td><td>Grey Ladies</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div>
</section>
